    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d334">

                <pb facs="0733" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1981-88v24/pg694"/>

                <head>334. Memorandum From Secretary of State Shultz to President Reagan<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d334-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1985-10-22">October 22, 1985</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1. <hi rendition="#italic">John Whitehead’s Meetings in Tunisia</hi>. In meetings
                    with the Tunisian Foreign Minister, Prime Minister and President
                        Bourguiba,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d334-f2"/> John got an earful of Tunisian
                    indignation about our perceived involvement in the Israeli raid on the PLO base
                    in Tunisia and our reaction to it. As the day went on, however, the atmosphere
                    of bitterness and resentment seemed to steadily improve. Although the Tunisians
                    are pessimistic about the peace process and continue to be bitter toward Israel,
                    all John’s interlocutors made strong pledges of continued friendship and
                    cooperation with the US. Significantly, they agreed that they will not allow Abu
                    Abbas into the country as long as there is any doubt at all about his
                    involvement in the hijacking.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d334-f3"/> All indications
                    are that the Tunisians consider the mission to have been a success. (S)</p>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to Tunisia.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
